---
import Book from "../layouts/Book.astro";
import data from "../data/skills.json";

const cmdCount = data.count;
const agentCount = 45;
const mcpCount = 4;
const siteRoutes = 12;
---

<Book
  title="Architecture"
  chapter="architecture"
  description="luna-agents system architecture in 3D — npm package, plugin, MCPs, site, Cloudflare edge. Interactive Three.js."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Chapter 09 · Architecture · 3D</p>
    <h1 class="title">The system, rotated.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      luna-agents is a layered system: an npm package that ships a
      Claude Code plugin, four MCP servers, an Astro book at
      agents.lunaos.ai, and a Cloudflare edge to serve all of it. Below
      is every piece in 3D. Drag to orbit. Scroll to zoom. Click a node
      to inspect.
    </p>
    <dl class="counters">
      <div><dt>Commands</dt><dd>{cmdCount}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Agents</dt><dd>{agentCount}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>MCP servers</dt><dd>{mcpCount}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Site routes</dt><dd>{siteRoutes}</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="canvas-wrap" aria-label="3D architecture diagram">
    <div id="arch-canvas" role="img" aria-label="Interactive 3D architecture of luna-agents"></div>
    <div id="arch-tooltip" hidden></div>
    <div class="legend" aria-label="Legend">
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#f4b942"></span>Plugin core</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#f6d476"></span>Commands</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#7ab8ff"></span>Agents</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#86d28f"></span>MCP servers</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#e8e2d4"></span>Site</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#f38020"></span>Cloudflare</div>
      <div><span class="dot" style="background:#9b8a7a"></span>External</div>
    </div>
    <p class="controls-hint" aria-hidden="true">drag · scroll · click</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Layers, in prose.</h2>

    <h3>1. Runtime entry</h3>
    <p>
      <code>npm install -g luna-agents</code> drops the <code>luna-setup</code>
      binary on your PATH. It detects Claude Code at
      <code>~/.claude</code> and registers the plugin marketplace, which
      makes every <code>/luna-agents:*</code> command available.
    </p>

    <h3>2. The plugin</h3>
    <p>
      <code>.claude-plugin/</code> is the Claude Code plugin
      manifest. It points at the sibling <code>commands/</code>
      directory ({cmdCount} markdown files, one per slash command) and
      <code>agents/</code> ({agentCount} agents). The whole bundle is
      versioned together as <code>luna-agents-marketplace</code>.
    </p>

    <h3>3. MCP servers</h3>
    <p>
      Four MCP servers sit in <code>mcp-servers/</code> and expose
      tools over stdio:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>luna-nexa-rag</code> — semantic code search powered by Nexa SDK embeddings</li>
      <li><code>luna-glm-vision</code> — GLM 4V image understanding for UI audits</li>
      <li><code>luna-vision-rag-client</code> — composes RAG + vision</li>
      <li><code>luna-lexicon</code> — exposes the {cmdCount}-entry lexicon over MCP</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4. The book (this site)</h3>
    <p>
      <code>site/</code> is an Astro static site deployed to
      Cloudflare Pages project <code>luna-agent</code> behind
      <a href="https://agents.lunaos.ai/">agents.lunaos.ai</a>. Each
      page in <a href="/">the book</a> is one Astro file under
      <code>site/src/pages/</code>.
    </p>

    <h3>5. Edge</h3>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Pages serves the static book. The wider LunaOS engine
      lives on Workers + D1 + KV + R2; the agents site doesn't depend
      on it at runtime — it's a static artifact.
    </p>

    <h2>How the 3D was built.</h2>
    <p>
      Three.js loaded from a CDN module. Nodes are
      <code>SphereGeometry</code> with emissive materials; connections
      are <code>Line</code> segments with particles travelling along
      them. Positions are hand-tuned to keep layers stacked left → right
      from <em>install</em> to <em>edge</em>. No physics simulation;
      determinism over noise.
    </p>
    <p>
      View source on <a href="https://github.com/lunaos-ai/luna-agents/blob/main/site/src/pages/architecture.astro">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Book>

<style>
  .hero { padding: var(--t-12) clamp(1rem, 5vw, 4rem) var(--t-6); }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--t-3);
  }
  .title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--t-3);
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 var(--t-3);
  }
  .counters {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--t-3) var(--t-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--t-3) 0;
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: var(--t-3) 0 0;
  }
  .counters dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-bottom: var(--t-1);
  }
  .counters dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step-1); }

  .canvas-wrap {
    position: relative;
    margin: var(--t-6) 0 var(--t-8);
    padding: 0;
    background: #0e0c0a;
    border-top: 1px solid #2a241c;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2a241c;
  }
  #arch-canvas {
    width: 100%;
    height: clamp(420px, 65vh, 720px);
    display: block;
    cursor: grab;
  }
  #arch-canvas:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  #arch-tooltip {
    position: absolute;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: rgba(20, 16, 12, 0.94);
    color: #f0ece4;
    border: 1px solid #3a2f24;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    max-width: 280px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    line-height: 1.4;
    z-index: 5;
  }
  #arch-tooltip strong { color: var(--saffron); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25em; }
  .legend {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1rem;
    left: 1rem;
    background: rgba(20,16,12,0.7);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    border: 1px solid #2a241c;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: #d4cdbf;
    z-index: 4;
  }
  .legend div { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5ch; }
  .legend .dot { width: 0.7rem; height: 0.7rem; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; box-shadow: 0 0 8px currentColor; }
  .controls-hint {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 1rem;
    right: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: #6e6557;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    z-index: 4;
  }

  section.wrap { padding: var(--t-6) 0 var(--t-12); }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--t-8); }
  h3 { margin-top: var(--t-6); }
  ul { max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  li code { color: var(--saffron-deep); }
</style>

<script type="module">
  import * as THREE from "https://esm.sh/three@0.169.0";
  import { OrbitControls } from "https://esm.sh/three@0.169.0/examples/jsm/controls/OrbitControls.js";

  const COMMANDS_COUNT = 285;
  const AGENTS_COUNT = 45;

  // Architecture model. Each layer is one X position; nodes spread on Y/Z.
  const NODES = [
    // Layer 0 — entry
    { id: "user",      label: "Developer",          group: "external", desc: "You. Runs `npm install` and types `/luna-agents:*` in Claude Code.", pos: [-9, 0, 0],  r: 0.9 },
    { id: "npm",       label: "npm registry",       group: "external", desc: "luna-agents@2.0.2 ships 401 files, ~500KB tarball.", pos: [-7, 1.6, 1.2], r: 0.7 },

    // Layer 1 — runtime
    { id: "setup",     label: "luna-setup",         group: "core",     desc: "The bin script. Idempotent installer. See setup.sh.", pos: [-5, 0, 0], r: 0.8 },
    { id: "cc",        label: "Claude Code",        group: "external", desc: "Host runtime. Loads the plugin via marketplace.", pos: [-5, -2, 1.5], r: 0.85 },

    // Layer 2 — plugin
    { id: "plugin",    label: ".claude-plugin",     group: "core",     desc: "Plugin manifest + marketplace.json. Versioned as luna-agents-marketplace.", pos: [-2, 0, 0], r: 1.1 },

    // Layer 3 — content (commands/agents/skills)
    { id: "commands",  label: `commands/ (${COMMANDS_COUNT})`, group: "commands", desc: `${COMMANDS_COUNT} slash commands. One markdown file each.`, pos: [1, 2, 0.5],   r: 1.0 },
    { id: "agents",    label: `agents/ (${AGENTS_COUNT})`,    group: "agents",   desc: `${AGENTS_COUNT} specialized agents (luna-hig, luna-no-bluf, luna-swarm, ...).`, pos: [1, -1.4, 0.5],  r: 0.9 },

    // Layer 4 — MCP
    { id: "rag",       label: "luna-nexa-rag",      group: "mcp",      desc: "Semantic code search over Nexa SDK embeddings. stdio MCP.", pos: [4, 2.5, -1.5], r: 0.75 },
    { id: "vision",    label: "luna-glm-vision",    group: "mcp",      desc: "GLM 4V image understanding for UI audits. stdio MCP.", pos: [4, 1, -2], r: 0.75 },
    { id: "vrclient",  label: "luna-vision-rag-client", group: "mcp",  desc: "Composes RAG + vision MCPs into one client.", pos: [4, -0.5, -1.5], r: 0.75 },
    { id: "lexicon",   label: "luna-lexicon",       group: "mcp",      desc: "Exposes the 285-entry lexicon over MCP.", pos: [4, -2, -2], r: 0.7 },

    // Layer 5 — site
    { id: "site",      label: "site/ (Astro)",      group: "site",     desc: "Static book. 12 pages: Lexicon, Skills, Showcase, Install, Play, Grammar, Etymology, Manifesto, Feedback, Architecture…", pos: [7, 1.5, 2], r: 1.0 },

    // Layer 6 — edge
    { id: "pages",     label: "Cloudflare Pages",   group: "edge",     desc: "Project: luna-agent. Custom domain: agents.lunaos.ai.", pos: [9.5, 0.5, 2.5], r: 0.85 },
    { id: "domain",    label: "agents.lunaos.ai",   group: "edge",     desc: "The book, served from the edge in 270+ cities.", pos: [11, -0.8, 2], r: 0.7 },
  ];

  const COLORS = {
    core:     0xf4b942,
    commands: 0xf6d476,
    agents:   0x7ab8ff,
    mcp:      0x86d28f,
    site:     0xe8e2d4,
    edge:     0xf38020,
    external: 0x9b8a7a,
  };

  const EDGES = [
    ["user", "npm", 0.3],
    ["npm", "setup", 0.8],
    ["user", "cc", 0.5],
    ["setup", "plugin", 0.9],
    ["cc", "plugin", 0.9],
    ["plugin", "commands", 1.0],
    ["plugin", "agents", 1.0],
    ["plugin", "rag", 0.6],
    ["plugin", "vision", 0.6],
    ["plugin", "vrclient", 0.6],
    ["plugin", "lexicon", 0.6],
    ["commands", "agents", 0.4],
    ["lexicon", "site", 0.5],
    ["site", "pages", 0.9],
    ["pages", "domain", 1.0],
    ["user", "domain", 0.3],
  ];

  const container = document.getElementById("arch-canvas");
  const tooltip = document.getElementById("arch-tooltip");
  if (!container || !tooltip) throw new Error("arch host missing");

  const reduced = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;

  const scene = new THREE.Scene();
  scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x0e0c0a);
  scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x0e0c0a, 18, 38);

  const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(45, container.clientWidth / container.clientHeight, 0.1, 100);
  camera.position.set(0, 4, 18);

  const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, alpha: false });
  renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));
  renderer.setSize(container.clientWidth, container.clientHeight);
  renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;
  renderer.toneMappingExposure = 1.15;
  container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

  const controls = new OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);
  controls.enableDamping = true;
  controls.dampingFactor = 0.08;
  controls.minDistance = 8;
  controls.maxDistance = 32;
  controls.autoRotate = !reduced;
  controls.autoRotateSpeed = 0.35;

  // Lighting
  scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.35));
  const key = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffe6c2, 0.9);
  key.position.set(8, 12, 8);
  scene.add(key);
  const fill = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0x88aaff, 0.35);
  fill.position.set(-10, -4, -6);
  scene.add(fill);

  // Subtle ground reflection
  const grid = new THREE.GridHelper(40, 40, 0x2a241c, 0x1a1612);
  grid.position.y = -4;
  scene.add(grid);

  // Nodes
  const nodeIndex = new Map();
  const nodeMeshes = [];
  for (const n of NODES) {
    const geo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(n.r, 36, 36);
    const color = COLORS[n.group] ?? 0xffffff;
    const mat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
      color,
      emissive: color,
      emissiveIntensity: 0.45,
      roughness: 0.4,
      metalness: 0.2,
    });
    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);
    mesh.position.set(...n.pos);
    mesh.userData = n;
    scene.add(mesh);

    // Halo
    const halo = new THREE.Mesh(
      new THREE.SphereGeometry(n.r * 1.55, 24, 24),
      new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color, transparent: true, opacity: 0.08, depthWrite: false })
    );
    mesh.add(halo);

    nodeIndex.set(n.id, mesh);
    nodeMeshes.push(mesh);
  }

  // Edges + particles
  const particles = [];
  for (const [a, b, intensity] of EDGES) {
    const ma = nodeIndex.get(a), mb = nodeIndex.get(b);
    if (!ma || !mb) continue;
    const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints([ma.position, mb.position]);
    const mat = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({
      color: 0xb89b6e,
      transparent: true,
      opacity: 0.15 + intensity * 0.25,
    });
    scene.add(new THREE.Line(geo, mat));

    // particle
    const pgeo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.08 + intensity * 0.05, 12, 12);
    const pmat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xffd17a });
    const p = new THREE.Mesh(pgeo, pmat);
    p.userData = { from: ma.position.clone(), to: mb.position.clone(), t: Math.random(), speed: 0.0025 + intensity * 0.003 };
    scene.add(p);
    particles.push(p);
  }

  // Picking
  const raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();
  const mouse = new THREE.Vector2();
  let hovered = null;

  function setMouseFromEvent(e) {
    const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();
    mouse.x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1;
    mouse.y = -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1;
    return rect;
  }

  function pick() {
    raycaster.setFromCamera(mouse, camera);
    const hits = raycaster.intersectObjects(nodeMeshes, false);
    return hits[0]?.object ?? null;
  }

  renderer.domElement.addEventListener("pointermove", (e) => {
    const rect = setMouseFromEvent(e);
    const hit = pick();
    if (hit !== hovered) {
      if (hovered) hovered.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.45;
      hovered = hit;
      if (hovered) hovered.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.95;
      renderer.domElement.style.cursor = hovered ? "pointer" : "grab";
    }
    if (hovered) {
      const n = hovered.userData;
      tooltip.innerHTML = `<strong>${n.label}</strong>${n.desc}`;
      tooltip.hidden = false;
      const tx = e.clientX - rect.left + 14;
      const ty = e.clientY - rect.top + 14;
      tooltip.style.left = tx + "px";
      tooltip.style.top = ty + "px";
    } else {
      tooltip.hidden = true;
    }
  });

  renderer.domElement.addEventListener("pointerleave", () => {
    if (hovered) hovered.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.45;
    hovered = null;
    tooltip.hidden = true;
  });

  renderer.domElement.addEventListener("click", () => {
    if (!hovered) return;
    controls.autoRotate = false;
    const target = hovered.position.clone();
    controls.target.lerp(target, 0.6);
  });

  // Resize
  function onResize() {
    const w = container.clientWidth, h = container.clientHeight;
    camera.aspect = w / h;
    camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
    renderer.setSize(w, h, false);
  }
  window.addEventListener("resize", onResize);

  // Animate
  function tick() {
    for (const p of particles) {
      const d = p.userData;
      d.t += d.speed;
      if (d.t > 1) d.t = 0;
      p.position.lerpVectors(d.from, d.to, d.t);
    }
    for (const m of nodeMeshes) {
      m.rotation.y += 0.003;
    }
    controls.update();
    renderer.render(scene, camera);
    requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  tick();
</script>
